     "reason": "Identify evidence that the paper's description of the implemented method, architecture, parameters, or execution materially contradicts the submitted code and run evidence. A missing artifact, unrun experiment, weak result, or unproven claim alone is insufficient.",
     "judge_reason": "The manuscript materially overstates the implemented archive coverage. It claims 27 distinct archived carbon settings and an exhaustive archive map, but the loader processes only gain_ files. The supplied fixed-detuning transfer tables contain 81 distinct carbon settings after zero-field deduplication, including 54 absent from the evaluation. The disclosed filename rule does not make the manuscript's exhaustive coverage claim accurate.",
     "evidence": [
      "proposal/sections/methods.tex:47-49 states that the archive contains 27 carbon settings and that every configuration is enumerated.",
      "proposal/sections/archive_results.tex:9, rendered in proposal/report.pdf page 5: 'The upper six panels contain every distinct archive configuration.'",
      "proposal/code/load_archive.py:16-34 loads only **/gain_*.txt; proposal/logs/evaluation.json contains 27 carbon evaluations.",
      "proposal/data/processed/PIC_processed_data/n3.5T800/phi75/transfer_real_zz_dL0.9.txt:6-14 specifies 0.9 Å and includes additional 50 T and 100 T settings, with gains 1.041413 and 1.049730. These are 0.5 and 1 MG, absent from the map and evaluation.",
      "The six supplied carbon transfer_real_*_dL0.9.txt files contain 81 distinct field/azimuth/polarization settings; only 27 occur in the evaluated set."
